; A LOOP VARIABLE FED FROM A WIDE ONE IS WIDE (irstep3-2026-09-25, the Java part).
; expect: 0 0 5000000000 7 7 7 7 7 7
;
; x takes y's previous value, and y reads the table. The Java term backend
; narrowed each loop variable to Java's `int` separately: a source that is
; ANOTHER loop variable counted as fitting by induction, even when that variable
; had itself been refused. So x was `int` and y `long`, the assignment was
; `x = (int) y`, and n = 2 answered 705032704, 5·10⁹ mod 2³². The induction
; holds only over the set of variables that all narrow, which is a greatest
; fixpoint. The IR's printer reads each range off its interval fixpoint, where
; x's range includes the element's.
(def run (n)
  (let a (array 5000000000 7 9)
    (loop ((i 0) (x 0) (y 0))
      (>= i (len a))  x
      (>= i n)        x
      else             (again (+ i 1) y (a i)))))
